  "details": "Something that people would probably be willing to pay for is having a world hosted on a low-latency server to allow competitive games. Current >200ms servers are a game breaker for most game worlds.\nA business model could include allowing people to \"boost\" a certain world (similar to how discord works) which then, in turn, makes them visible as a booster in that world. \nx boosts could mean n instances with low latency (or n users), so more boosts per month means more low latency instances for that world.",
